# In-flight work guard

**Invariant:** `dispatch_active(work) ∧ overlap(in_seat_work, work) ⇒ halt(in_seat)` ·
`¬abort(session) ∧ ¬cancel(dispatch) ∧ ¬kill(execution)` — unless the operator **names** the override
("abort the dispatch", "cancel 6488", "implement in IDE, don't wait for SDK"). Tier change, urgency,
slow polls, "session looked stale", and CHECKPOINT next-step changes are **not** authorization.

Active = `execution_id` / `dispatch_id` returned and not terminal · `poll_hint` open for `from_agent=cursor-sdk` ·
thread shows admit without terminal closeout · scoreboard marks the slice IN FLIGHT. Overlap = same **work
identity** (`work_key` = `todo:{slug}`; `source_ref` fallback — conductor rows carry none), `packet_path`, or
`files_expected` loci; the live conductor `dispatch_id` is the **holder** named in the 409, not the key. Lane B
worktrees do not lift the guard on the same paths.

## Forbidden / Permitted

| Forbidden | Permitted |
|---|---|
| Edit paths the dispatch owns; "head start while SDK runs" | Poll `agent_bus.wait` / read thread / harvest closeout; edits **outside** the overlap |
| Cancel queued cursor-sdk "as cleanup"; tear down a converse lane / live CSE | Author the packet **before** firing; lead verify **after** terminal closeout |
| Infer "no active CDP" from empty `active_work` while the private request lane runs | Read the private request thread — transport idle ≠ bus idle |
| Hop / re-stream / refuse PARK to "keep the tab alive" | PARK; tab ⟂ session (`decision:cse-tab-decoupled-from-session`) |

Closing an agent-bus thread ≠ aborting substrate work. Abort of a transport handle ≢ abort of the
operator-proxy arc (commission lives on the private request lane). Dead `execution_id` is not reopenable —
continuity is the request thread; `cse_session(op=followup)` may reattach.

